          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "A spin-off of Hudson's Peach Boy RPG series that focuses on three side characters instead.\n\nMomotarou Densetsu Gaiden (\"Peach Boy Legend Side-Story\"), known as Momotarou Densetsu Gaiden: Dai 1-Shu (\"Peach Boy Legend Side-Story: Volume 1\") for PC Engine, is a non-core entry in Hudson's Momotarou Densetsu series of RPGs loosely inspired by the titular folklore figure. It was first released on the Game Boy in 1991, and then ported to the PC Engine the next year and the Famicom the year following that.\n\nThe game switches focus from Momotarou to three extra characters, each has their own distinct campaign to play through. One follows a standard RPG route of a hero's journey, another involves the princess of the kingdom of demons as she attempts to uncover an attack on her father's throne with a band of allied monsters, and the third involves a thief who steals money from monsters and gives it to beggars. Each campaign follows the core gameplay of the series: overworld exploration and turn-based combat.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Una spin-off de la serie de RPG Peach Boy de Hudson, que se centra en tres personajes secundarios en su lugar.\n\nMomotarou Densetsu Gaiden (\"Peach Boy Legend Side-Story\"), conocido como Momotarou Densetsu Gaiden: Dai 1-Shu (\"Peach Boy Legend Side-Story: Volume 1\") en PC Engine, es una entrega no principal de la serie de RPG Momotarou Densetsu de Hudson, vagamente inspirada en la figura del folclore que da título a la serie. Se lanzó por primera vez en Game Boy en 1991, y luego se portó a PC Engine al año siguiente y a Famicom el año posterior.\n\nEl juego cambia el foco de Momotarou a tres personajes adicionales, cada uno con su propia campaña. Una sigue la ruta típica de un RPG, el viaje de un héroe; otra involucra a la princesa del reino de los demonios, que intenta descubrir un ataque contra el trono de su padre junto a un grupo de monstruos aliados; y la tercera trata de un ladrón que roba dinero a los monstruos y se lo entrega a los mendigos. Cada campaña sigue la jugabilidad básica de la serie: exploración del mundo y combates por turnos.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1991",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
